<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaamba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chaamba tribe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chaamba are an Arabic-speaking nomadic tribal confederation of the northern Algerian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, centred on the region of Ouargla, Metlili and El Golea. They herded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a>, traded and controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a>, and dealt with the oasis towns of the region. In the 19th century many Chaamba served the French as camel troops in the conquest of the Sahara.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chaamba.jpg" alt="Chaamba" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chaamba_riding_a_camel_in_southern_Tunisia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
